===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|literary}} {{non-gloss definition|Used, especially at a [[parting#Noun|parting]], to [[express#Verb|express]] the [[wish#Noun|wish]] that the [[outcome]] of the [[action#Noun|actions]] of a [[person#Noun|person]] (typically someone about to [[start#Verb|start]] a [[journey#Noun|journey]] or a [[daring#Adjective|daring]] [[endeavor#Noun|endeavour]]) is [[positive#Adjective|positive]] for them.}}
#: {{synonyms|en|all the best|q2=archaic|fare thee well|farewell|goodbye|good luck}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3|act=II|scene=iii|page=184|column=2|passage=''3'' [''Citizen'']. Neighbours, '''God ſpeed'''. / ''1'' [''Citizen'']. Giue you good morrovv ſir.}}
#* {{RQ:Dekker Dramatic Works|volume=II|title=Honest Whore|act=I|scene=i|page=80|passage=''Duke''. '''God ſpeed''' father. / ''1. Mad''[''man'']. God ſpeed the Plough, thou ſhalt not ſpeed me.}}
#* {{RQ:Gandhi Experiments|volume=I|chapter=Preparation for England|page=95|passage=At the threshold of death, how dare I give you permission to go to England, to cross the seas? But I will not stand in your way. It is your mother's permission which really matters. If she permit you, then '''godspeed'''! Tell her I will not interfere. You will go with my blessings.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|quotee={{w|Scott Carpenter}}|title=Godspeed, John Glenn|newspaper={{w|USA Today}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210709041613/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/2016/12/08/short-list-thursday/95136358/|location=McLean, Va.|publisher=[[w:Gannett|Gannett Co.]]|date=20 February 1962|year_published=8 December 2016|issn=0734-7456|oclc=658972642|passage=So all of America watched at 9:47 a.m. on Feb. 20, 1962, as [[w:John Glenn|[John] Glenn]] took off from Cape Canaveral. Scott Carpenter, backup astronaut for the mission, famously said: "'''Godspeed''', John Glenn."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Peter Steinfels|authorlink=Peter Steinfels|title=At commencement, a call for religious literacy|newspaper={{w|The New York Times}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221126035128/https://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/12/us/12beliefs.html|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|The New York Times Company}}|date=12 May 2007|issn=0362-4331|oclc=971436363|passage=So, class of 2007, join in. And '''godspeed'''.}}

