===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}} {{term-label|en|literary}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[wish#Verb|wishing]] of someone a [[smooth#Adjective|smooth]] [[journey#Noun|journey]], or [[success]], especially at a [[parting#Noun|parting]]; {{lb|en|countable}} a [[statement#Noun|statement]] [[express#Verb|expressing]] this.
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|book=2 John|verses=10–11|folio=ccc|passage=Yff there come eny vnto you and brynge not this learnynge&#11805; hym receave not to houſſe: nether bid hym '''god ſpede'''. For he that biddeth hym '''God ſpede'''&#11805; is part taker off his evyll dedes.}}
#* {{RQ:Bunyan Pilgrim's Progress|page=18|passage=Then ''Chriſtian'' took his leave of his Friend, and he again bid him '''God ſpeed'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Vanbrugh Relapse|scene=ii|page=90|passage=''Ber''[''inthia'']. Speed her vvell. / ''VVor''[''thy'']. Ay, but there muſt be more than a '''God ſpeed''', or your Charity vvon't be vvorth a farthing.}}
#* {{RQ:Anne Bronte Tenant|volume=I|chapter=The Warnings of Experience|page=279|passage=He never danced himself, and there he sat, poking his head in my face, and impressing all the beholders with the idea that he was a confirmed, acknowledged lover; my aunt looking complacently on, all the time, and wishing him '''God-speed'''.}}
#* {{RQ:James Roderick Hudson|page=28|passage=[I]n the morning, as Rowland at the garden gate was giving his hostess '''Godspeed''' on her way to church, he came striding along the grassy margin of the road and out-whistling the music of the church bells.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Thon|journal=The Critic and Good Literature|date=1884-11-02|issue=44|page=210|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=9H_mAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA210|oclc=|passage=The new word has received a number of '''godspeeds''', some of which we quote.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Eight years before he had seen his friend off at the North Wall and wished him '''God-speed'''.|author=James Joyce|title=Dubliners|year=1914}}
# {{lb|en|countable|figuratively}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} ''Chiefly in'' '''in the Godspeed of''': the most [[important]] [[part#Noun|part]] of something, or [[point#Noun|point]] at which something [[happen]]s; also, the [[last minute]] or [[last#Adjective|last]] [[moment]].
## {{lb|en|originally|Ireland}} ''In'' '''[[back of Godspeed]]''': a [[distant]], [[remote#Adjective|remote]], or [[unknown#Adjective|unknown]] [[place#Noun|place]].
##: {{synonyms|en|back of beyond}}

